,"default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-01-06T18:25:38Z","updated_at":"2025-01-13T09:53:37Z","closed_at":"2025-01-13T00:36:18Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in: 4.3dev\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.22631 - GLES3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4050 Laptop GPU (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.6070) - Intel(R) Core(TM) Ultra 7 155H (22 Threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nCreating a GUI in which content scale factor is used to achieve resolution independent scaling.\n\nI have a basic setup with a control node full rect and a bottom anchored set of control panels.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2a39009d-0103-49a0-a148-2b490d5dc3b1)\n\nWhen changing content scale factor, the nodes grow inwards until they meet each other by the horizontal separation of `90` which I've set. Beyond this point they will stretch outside their parent container and control node beyond the screen bounds.\n\nI've managed to reproduce this without changing content scale factor and by only setting the minimum size of the two panels. Decreasing the scale of the parent control node by the factor of its size to the screen resolution seems to ignore the FULL rect anchor property.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cadf695c-a5c2-44fa-8023-1d3151e11137)\n\nWhat I would expect to happen is that when the two panels at the bottom meet horizontally, they will continue to grow vertically but not grow beyond the screen width. Until they've hit the screen height in which case content scale factor would have no further effect.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nN/A minimal example given above\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"RobertBColton","id":3212801,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMTI4MDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3212801?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton","html_url":"https://github.com/RobertBColton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobertBColton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101188/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101188/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}